---
import ServicePageLayout from '../layouts/ServicePageLayout.astro';
import { faqsBySlug } from '../data/faqs';

const slug = 'customs-support-singapore';
---

<ServicePageLayout
  slug={slug}
  metaTitle="Customs Support Singapore | Import & Declaration Coordination"
  metaDescription="Help understanding customs and declaration requirements for a Singapore import. We help you prepare, coordinate, and connect with appropriate support before your shipment needs to clear."
  breadcrumbLabel="Customs support"
  eyebrow="Customs & import coordination"
  h1="Customs support for Singapore imports"
  lede="For businesses that are unsure what a shipment needs before it clears customs — what a permit involves, what a Declaring Agent will ask for, and how to prepare in advance."
  faqs={faqsBySlug[slug]}
  whatsappMessage="Hi CargoAdvisor, I need help understanding customs requirements for an import into Singapore."
>
  <section class="section section--border-top" aria-labelledby="reality-heading">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="eyebrow">How this works in Singapore</div>
      <h2 id="reality-heading">A brief, honest overview of the process</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        We want to be precise here rather than vague, because customs mistakes are expensive to unwind.
        In Singapore, import permit applications are submitted through <strong>TradeNet</strong>, the
        national single window for trade declarations. To use it, a business generally needs a{' '}
        <strong>UEN</strong> and an activated <strong>Customs Account</strong> with Singapore Customs.
        From there, many businesses appoint a <strong>Declaring Agent</strong> — a party authorised to
        submit the permit application on their behalf — rather than applying directly.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        CargoAdvisor.sg is not positioning itself as a licensed Declaring Agent unless explicitly stated
        for a specific engagement. What we do is help you understand what applies to your shipment,
        prepare the information a declaration is likely to need, and connect you with appropriate support
        for the parts that require a licensed party.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--subtle section--border-top" aria-labelledby="help-with-heading">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="eyebrow">Where we help</div>
      <h2 id="help-with-heading">What "customs support" covers here</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: var(--step-0); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700;">Before you ship</h3>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-2);">
            Helping you assess whether a permit is likely to apply, and what invoice, packing list, and
            product details you should have ready in advance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: var(--step-0); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700;">Getting set up</h3>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-2);">
            If you don’t yet have a UEN or Customs Account, we help you understand the sequence of steps
            involved before a permit can be applied for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: var(--step-0); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700;">Connecting you to declaring support</h3>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-2);">
            Where a formal TradeNet declaration is required, we help connect you with appropriate,
            appropriately licensed support for that step.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: var(--step-0); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700;">Coordinating around the paperwork</h3>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--space-2);">
            Aligning the physical shipment — delivery timing, access, and handling — with what the
            documentation side needs, so nothing stalls at the last mile.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-faint" style="font-size: var(--step--1); margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        This page is a general overview, not legal or regulatory advice. Requirements vary by goods
        category and current regulation — always confirm specifics for your shipment during the
        guided enquiry or directly with Singapore Customs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServicePageLayout>
